\newlabel{tab:main}{{1}{5}{Main synthetic results at $n=500,N=10{,}000$. Each entry is mean width / coverage in percent (3,000 repetitions). These are not equal-validity width rankings: CP procedures have finite-sample guarantees under assumptions; Wald procedures are asymptotic. Complete MC uncertainty is in Appendix~\ref {app:allresults}}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Coverage (top) and width (bottom) on three prespecified laws. Coverage bars are pointwise Wilson MC95; width bars are $1.96$ MCSE. Exact construction costs precision on affine data, exploits sharp nonlinear information, and avoids the rare-event Wald collapse. Near-invisible width bars reflect precise MC means, not certainty about future scientific populations.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:main}{{1}{5}{Coverage (top) and width (bottom) on three prespecified laws. Coverage bars are pointwise Wilson MC95; width bars are $1.96$ MCSE. Exact construction costs precision on affine data, exploits sharp nonlinear information, and avoids the rare-event Wald collapse. Near-invisible width bars reflect precise MC means, not certainty about future scientific populations}{figure.1}{}}
